    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize math practice by adapting to student levels, like generating step-by-step solutions for algebra problems. They can also explain concepts in relatable terms, such as comparing calculus to gardening slopes. For schools, they could offer instant feedback on homework, reducing frustration and helping students build confidence gradually."
